                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One of the best *Resident Evil* games—if not the best. It never gets boring; it’s packed with plenty of solid puzzles and genuine horror moments. While it may be less frightening than *Resident Evil 7*, it still holds its own. The segments where you play as Chris are an absolute blast—the game really hits its stride toward the end. The finale is very satisfying, albeit a bit sad. The story frequently throws in interesting twists and turns.\n\nDimitrescu: A fairly easy encounter; her area is engaging rather than tedious, and the boss fight itself is quite enjoyable.\n\nBeneviento: The easiest section, regardless of the difficulty setting—it’s focused entirely on puzzles and leans more into horror.\n\nMoreau: This section goes by quite quickly, though the boss fight itself is actually rather challenging.\n\nHeisenberg: The most compelling \"Lord.\" His factory is a complex, difficult area—on the \"Hardcore\" difficulty, you’ll want to avoid some of the enemies entirely. The chaos that unfolds in the village is truly terrifying.\n\nMiranda: The conclusion to the story, featuring the longest—and arguably the most difficult—boss fight.\n\nIt’s crucial to keep a good supply of ammo and other consumables throughout most of the game. You’ll need them to survive the factory, as you’ll be forced to face a gauntlet—the Sturm (mini-boss), Heisenberg, and Miranda—one after another, with almost no time to catch your breath.\n\n10/10",
                        "timestamp_created": 1792414573,
